environment.description:
[ENVIRONMENT INFO:
Name: SUCC campus (Supernatural University of Central California);
Domain: Collegiate Supernatural Sanctuary & Academic Domain;
Coordinates & Span: 129 Hocus Way, coastal Solarton, California;
Setting & Metaphysics: Historic premier higher-education campus founded in 1887; balanced human-supernatural integration;
Dominant Presence: University Board of Regents, Student Body (8,000 students, 60/40 supernatural/human), Greek Row (10 houses), Faculty, DCC Fellows]

[LORE & ENVIRONMENT:
Atmosphere & Senses: Salty sea breeze mingled with coffee from The Roasted Bean, old parchment, ozone from arcane labs, freshly cut athletic turf;
Spatial Architecture: Collegiate gothic stone halls, arched cloisters, modern bioengineering glass cubes, Greek Row mansions, St. Neptune athletic complex;
Rifts & Dimensional Drift: Heavily anchored runic boundary wards preventing unauthorized dimensional tears on campus grounds;
Hazards & Rules: Strict scent suppressor compliance in lecture halls, mandatory neutral truce across rival houses and packs, no lethal dueling]

[CONTEXT & SECRETS:
Cosmology & Origins: Established to foster peaceful co-existence and academic mastery between supernatural lineages and mortals;
Secrets: The subterranean Basilica library basement (Room 005) hides forgotten pre-treaty pact archives and covert summoning circles]

location.description:
[LOCATION INFO:
Era: 2024 (Modern Fantasy / Post-Gate Era);
Location: Bulls Stadium / St. Neptune Athletic Complex (Athletic Sector, SUCC Campus);
Setting: Colossal multi-sport university stadium and athletic training complex, home of the SUCC Bulls;
Factions: SUCC Athletic Department, Bulls Football Team, Athletic Boosters, Student Pep Club;
Conflicts: High-intensity physical sports violence between supernatural athletes vs maintaining intercollegiate rules;
Society: Boisterous school spirit, athletic pride, intense training discipline, legendary game-day tailgates]

[LORE & ENVIRONMENT:
Environment: Roaring cheers from thousands of fans, smell of roasted peanuts, stadium hot dogs, fresh turf, and athletic liniment;
Architecture: Monumental open-air concrete and steel stadium bowl, towering LED floodlight towers, synthetic impact-resistant turf;
Security & Wards: Crowd control wards, physical kinetic dampeners absorbing stray shockwaves from super-strength tackles;
Demographics: Student athletes, coach Dullahan, enthusiastic fans, campus marching band, visiting collegiate rivals;
Rules & Restrictions: Zero unsanctioned magical curses targeting rival players on the field, respect referee whistles]

[CONTEXT & SECRETS:
History: Named in honor of St. Neptune, serving for decades as the beating heart of collegiate athletic dominance in California;
Secrets: The home team locker room features an enchanted hydro-massage recovery plunge that rapidly knits bruised muscle tissue]
